The FIRST A15 failed, structurally, not by a slip: mine() builds `head`
from the mining graph, so a rule whose conclusions live entirely in the
scored set is never a CANDIDATE. Not scored badly. Never considered.
Planting 100% of conclusions into held-out guaranteed NOT RECOVERED for
a rule present by construction. Had I shipped it, G22 would have read
"NO DISCOVERY, control beats treatment" -- the right verdict through a
blind instrument, indistinguishable in the output from the real thing.
That is the third time in a week. Same species as your residency point:
the check was exact and rested on something that could not speak.

-- THE EXPLANATION I WROTE, AND WHY IT WAS THE WRONG KIND --

I wrote: "a materialised deduction carries no information, derived is a
function of train, so a 2-hop rule over train+derived is a longer-path
rule over train reached badly."

Fitted to the number. Exactly the shape of my withdrawn "exact bound
1021, head plus wrapper". Plausible, unfalsified, and arrived at by
looking at a result and reaching for a story.

-- THE STRUCTURAL EXPLANATION, WHICH IS BETTER AND WAS FREE --

G22 satisfied ZERO of Lewontin's three conditions.

  variation             none. Derived edges are a DETERMINISTIC function
                        of train. One outcome. No population.
  heredity              trivial. Graph persists, nothing reproduces with
                        modification.
  differential fitness  none. Every top-k rule written, none removed,
                        nothing competes for anything finite.

It was deduction plus re-reading, wearing the word "evolution". A system
with none of the three is not expected to adapt and did not. I did not
need the experiment to predict that; I needed to have checked the
definition against the design before spending a day on it.

-- G24: BUILD THE THREE CONDITIONS AND ABLATE EACH ONE --

  genotype    rule = (body predicate tuple, head predicate)
  variation   swap / extend / contract / rehead / recombine / duplicate
  heredity    population persists, offspring carry parent body with one edit
  death       ECAN as a FINITE ECONOMY -- fixed wage pool shared each
              round, rent per body predicate AND per 1000 predictions
              asserted, importance <= 0 removes the rule
  problem     fitness against unanswered dev queries, not the graph at large
  waves       activation spreads from unsolved problems, multiplies wages
              in high-activation regions, recomputed each round so it MOVES
  adversary   reshuffled every round, best-of-m chosen to MAXIMISE the
              population's score. A static null gets memorised. Red Queen.

ECAN belongs here and I had it in the wrong place for the whole G-series.
G5/G19 used rent as memory management, to stop the space growing. Wrong
frame. RENT IS THE CARRYING CAPACITY THAT MAKES FITNESS DIFFERENTIAL.
With unlimited room, fitness differences do nothing at all.

-- THREE FAILURES ON THE WAY, EACH ONE A REAL PROPERTY --

1. A15 was IN the seed population. "A15 yes" at round 0, before a single
   mutation. A positive control that starts inside the thing it tests is
   not a control. Banned it from the seed.

2. THE FITNESS LANDSCAPE IS FLAT. A rule either clears MIN_PAIRS support
   or scores nothing -- no partial credit, so no slope. Uniform mutation
   over 237 predicates has nothing to climb. Fixed with structure-biased
   proposals in both directions (what follows p, what precedes q), which
   is mutational bias and is the genotype-phenotype map doing its job.

3. FITNESS REWARDED HITS AND NEVER CHARGED FOR BREADTH. Population
   evolved rules that assert everything: coverage up, precision 0.021 ->
   0.011. Added rent per 1000 predictions asserted. Pay for your claims.

-- THE OPERATOR'S POINT WAS THE ONE THAT MATTERED --

They said the system needs a problem space and adversarial learning
propagating in waves. The problem space turned out not to be a scoreboard
item. It is a VARIATION OPERATOR.

Every mutation operator above is blind: mutate, then discover relevance.
Abduction runs the other way -- take a problem the population cannot
solve, find a path between its endpoints in train, propose the rule that
path implies. Bottom-up clause construction, the ILP move.

  without abduction   A15 never found, test coverage +180
  with abduction      A15 found at round 3, test coverage +2892

Same everything else. That is the difference between a population that
drifts and one that searches.

-- WHAT I AM NOT CLAIMING --

Precision is BAD and falling (0.021 -> 0.013) while coverage rises 4x.
The population is buying recall with breadth and the rent-per-claim did
not stop it. Coverage without precision is not truth, and I am not going
to report the +2892 as a win until the precision curve is explained.

Also: I tuned the system until A15 fired. Every change was principled and
each one is documented in the file, but the control fired AFTER the
tuning rather than before, which makes it a weaker check than one that
fires first try. Recording that rather than letting it read as a clean
pass.

Full arms run (full / no_variation / no_abduct / no_death / static_adv /
no_waves) is running now. G23, whether depth-3 mining beats its OWN null,
is running alongside -- each depth against its own baseline, because
depth-3 searches a much larger rule space and comparing raw top-12 across
depths would be the same lenient comparison that has fired on noise three
times here.

