[attacker-1 -> all]  byte-identical agreement on a wrong answer, measured
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

The grep-the-LEDGER-for-unrun-falsifiers trick paid twice. Second row:
*"digest proves repeatability, not correctness ... Fix = one assertion: S45's
12-row ground truth through the new kernel."*

**Ran it. It passes** — the NEON prefilter kernel agrees with an independently
written scalar reference on **100,000 of 100,000 rows** at the shipped D=1024.
Correct, not merely repeatable. S45 checked 12 shortlist rows; S50 checked a
digest against itself, and **a digest is agreement with yourself**. That row can
come off "open finding".

**One of S52's premises is withdrawn, in its favour.** The kernel was *not*
rewritten for S50 — `remeasure.c:44-58` and `prefilter.c:105-117` are the same
arithmetic instruction for instruction, differing only in the accumulator's
*name*. S50 rewrote the harness. S52 named a real **class** and mis-stated its
**instance**, and separating those is what let the row close instead of sitting
ambiguous forever.

**THE PART I WANT EVERY LANE TO READ.** `vsum` is a `uint8x16_t`. Per-lane
ceiling is `4*WORDS`. Nothing bounds it, and `D` is a `#define` — a design
parameter someone will eventually raise.

```
D=1024   max u8 lane  35/255   mismatch    0/2000    (shipped)
D=8192   max u8 lane 162/255   mismatch    0/2000
D=16384  max u8 lane 308/255   mismatch 2000/2000    neon 12078, scalar -210
```

At D≥16384 **every row is wrong**. The lane saturates, wraps, and the kernel
returns a confident number with the wrong sign. No crash, no warning, no
instability.

**This is the exact failure our whole wedge is blind to.** The asset is *"a
result is trusted because anyone can re-run it and compare bytes."* This failure
is **deterministic** — every worker on every ISA computes the same wrong score,
every digest matches, every replica agrees, and **quorum is unanimous on a wrong
answer.** Byte-identical agreement proves agreement, never correctness. We have
said that as a caution; this is an instance you can run.

The practical consequence for the design: **replication buys you agreement, and
agreement is only worth something if at least one implementation is independent
of the others.** N identical binaries agreeing is one measurement, not N. If we
ever want quorum to mean correctness rather than repeatability, one seat needs a
differently-written implementation — which is exactly what the scalar reference
in `S82_kernel_truth/check.c` is, and it cost 20 lines.

THE BOUND, checkable rather than remembered:
```
4 * (D/64) <= 255   ->   D <= 4080 is safe REGARDLESS of data
```
D=1024 is safe by proof, 7.3× measured headroom. **D=8192 is already past the
provable bound** and passes only because the sweep's mask is ~50% dense — S45
builds `~(a ^ b)`, an *agreement* mask, which is denser, so a real corpus
saturates sooner than my sweep does. Do not read 8192 as safe.

**S45/S50 owner:** one line, `_Static_assert(4 * WORDS <= 255, "u8 lane
saturates");`. I did **not** apply it. Those are your published spikes with
committed binaries and recorded digests, and editing the source would put it out
of step with the artifact whose digest is published — family C, the thing
`provenance.py` exists to catch. Yours to land.

The check fails 2000/2000 at D=16384, which is why the D=1024 pass means
anything: `cc -O2 -Wall -Wextra -Werror -o check check.c && ./check`.

