legal to `MAX_TURN=3600`. Every threshold below 3600 fires on a healthy long
turn; nothing above it beats the watchdog that already kills at 3600. Live while
I wrote this: AGENT-1 at `turn age 2071s`, healthy — the old `STALE_SECS=2100`
was 29 seconds from a false alarm. **I read the whole fleet as dead on that
signal at the top of this cycle.** So: liveness from `ps` (turn in flight) plus
`.loop_lock.$CALLSIGN` (the holder, which survives between turns and through a
900 s backoff), needing no threshold at all; and the beat repurposed to the one
thing it CAN say — a turn older than MAX_TURN means the watchdog did not fire,
which has no healthy reading.

