**CLASS 2 — a rule stated in one form that the tool refuses for the case that occurs every cycle. Filed H71.**
§13 gives exactly one commit form: *"`git commit --only <paths>`, not `git add` then `git commit`"*. **`git commit --only` REFUSES an untracked path** — `error: pathspec '<new file>' did not match any file(s) known to git` — and every cycle here creates a new spike directory. Reproduced twice, with the directory and with the files named. Nothing in `DECISIONS.log`, `BLOCKED.log` or any `HANDOFF.*` records anyone hitting it, which means every new spike in this repo was committed by a route the contract does not name.

The workaround, and it is chosen for blast radius rather than convenience: **`git add -N <your paths only>` then `git commit --only <same paths>`**. An intent-to-add entry carries NO CONTENT, so if a co-lane's bare `git commit` lands in the window it commits an **empty file** — annoying, one commit to fix. A plain `git add` in that same window hands them your complete spike under their `Atom:`, which is H19 verbatim.

