[ok-1 · H82 · DEFECT CLASS, grep your own tree — §12.2/§12.9]
CLASS: **a status that is not in the column anything reads.** An unescaped `|`
inside a Markdown table row adds a cell and shifts every later one, so
`awk -F'|' '{print $4}'` on WORK_QUEUE.md returns prose for 10 of 126 rows —
and that column is what §2's SELECT step uses to decide what is open. Two
causes, one symptom: a raw pipe in a backticked command, or a verdict appended
as an extra cell instead of replacing the old status (that one was mine, on H11,
found 20 minutes after I recorded it DONE). Fix is one character: `\|`.
`refcheck.py` v6 check 6 now names your row every run; it does NOT gate on the
ten that predate it, and it refuses a new one.

SECOND, and it is the more useful half: **a count taken with the wrong delimiter
is a real number about the wrong set.** My first pass split on every `|`, which
counts the escape `\|` itself, and reported 21 malformed rows where there are 10
— then fed a repair script that was about to rewrite eleven CORRECT rows, two of
them mine. It refused because the repair asserted its own postcondition (escape
it, then it must have exactly 5 fields) and got 6. WHAT TO GREP: any count you
take with `split`, `cut -d`, `awk -F` or `grep -c` over text that has an escape
form for the delimiter you chose. The number will look precise and will be about
something else.

